</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Compatibility with Other RL Algorithm</h2>

<figure id="A3.F12" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2604.03098v1/dapo_training_curve.svg" id="A3.F12.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:384/234;" width="384" height="234"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 12: </span>Training curves of DAPO and DAPO w/ SG &amp; GR. Our method achieves a final success rate of 78.1% vs. 72.2% for the DAPO baseline.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Although we instantiate our method on top of GRPO throughout the main experiments, the proposed Self-Guidance &amp; Guidance reward training mechanism is not specific to a single RL algorithm. Our method modifies the training signal by introducing self-guidance and an additional guidance reward, while leaving the underlying policy optimization algorithm unchanged. This makes it naturally compatible with other GRPO-family or outcome-driven RL algorithms.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To test this, we additionally apply our method on top of <span id="A3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DAPO</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yu et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, replacing vanilla GRPO with the DAPO objective while keeping the same Self-Guidance &amp; Guidance reward design. We train Qwen3-1.7B on WebShop for <span id="A3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">100</span> epochs with a group size of <span id="A3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">8</span>, learning rate <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math>, KL coefficient <span id="A3.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">0.01</span>, and DAPO clip ratios <span id="A3.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(0.2,0.28)</span>; the guidance reward is introduced at step <span id="A3.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">40</span>. As shown in Figure <a href="#A3.F12" title="Figure 12 ‣ Appendix C Compatibility with Other RL Algorithm ‣ Co-Evolution of Policy and Internal Reward for Language Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>, once the guidance reward is introduced at step 40, our method begins to pull ahead of the DAPO baseline and maintains a higher success rate through the remainder of training, resulting in a stronger final performance. This suggests that the benefit of learned self-guidance and guidance reward is complementary to the choice of the underlying RL algorithm rather than being tied to GRPO alone.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Details of Offline Self-Guidance Model Distillation</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section provides additional details for the offline self-guidance distillation alternative discussed in Section <a href="#S4.SS5" title="4.5 Ablation on Co-Evolution ‣ 4 Experiments, Results, and Analysis ‣ Co-Evolution of Policy and Internal Reward for Language Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Setup and Distillation Objective</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conduct the offline distillation experiment on ALFWorld. The student self-guidance model is Qwen3-1.7B, and the teacher is a stronger Qwen3-32B model. For each trajectory prefix, the student observes only the prefix up to step <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and produces a rating for the current state. The teacher is given the full trajectory in hindsight and evaluates the student output using the complete rollout outcome. We instantiate both teacher and student within the Qwen3 family to reduce additional mismatch from heterogeneous model families, so that the main gap comes from context and capability rather than architecture differences.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For each trajectory prefix, the student produces a rating using the same prompt defined in <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Experiment Details ‣ Co-Evolution of Policy and Internal Reward for Language Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>. The teacher scores the student output using the full trajectory in hindsight and returns a scalar reward in <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, which serves as the supervision signal for offline distillation. The exact prompt template is shown in Figure <a href="#A4.F13" title="Figure 13 ‣ D.1 Setup and Distillation Objective ‣ Appendix D Details of Offline Self-Guidance Model Distillation ‣ Co-Evolution of Policy and Internal Reward for Language Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F13" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A4.F13.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="766.53" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 522.5 766.53" width="522.5"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,766.53) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 16.85 L 0 749.68 C 0 758.99 7.55 766.53 16.85 766.53 L 505.64 766.53 C 514.95 766.53 522.5 758.99 522.5 749.68 L 522.5 16.85 C 522.5 7.55 514.95 0 505.64 0 L 16.85 0 C 7.55 0 0 7.55 0 16.85 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 16.85 L 1.11 744.15 L 521.39 744.15 L 521.39 16.85 C 521.39 8.16 514.34 1.11 505.64 1.11 L 16.85 1.11 C 8.16 1.11 1.11 8.16 1.11 16.85 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.79 751.88)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:30.23em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="418.3"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A4.F13.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:30.23em;">
<span id="A4.F13.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F13.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Prompt Template for Offline Self-Guidance Distillation</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.79 15.61)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:34.76em;--ltx-fo-height:51.8em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="719.42" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 716.73)" width="480.98"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A4.F13.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:34.76em;">
<span id="A4.F13.pic1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.F13.pic1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F13.pic1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are an expert hindsight judge for action-observation trajectories.</span></span>
<span id="A4.F13.pic1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F13.pic1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You will be given:</span></span>
<span id="A4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">FULL trajectory: initial observation, task, steps </span><math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\dots T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\dots T</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and outcome.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Student output for step </span><math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: (ignore the thinking part) two lines: </span><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Reason: ...</span><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Label: negative|neutral|positive</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A4.F13.pic1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F13.pic1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Your job:</span></span>
<span id="A4.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<span id="A4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<span id="A4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Decide whether the student’s </span><span id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">LABEL</span><span id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is correct in hindsight (use the full trajectory; events after step </span><math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> are allowed).</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<span id="A4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Produce a scalar reward in </span><math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:</span></span>
<span id="A4.I2.i2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">exact label match </span><math id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> about </span><math id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+0.8</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">adjacent mismatch (positive</span><math id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftrightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">↔</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftrightarrow</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">neutral or neutral</span><math id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftrightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">↔</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftrightarrow</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">negative) </span><math id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> about </span><math id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+0.2</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">opposite mismatch (positive</span><math id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftrightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">↔</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftrightarrow</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">negative) </span><math id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> about </span><math id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-0.8</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">invalid format/label </span><math id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow-1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1.0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow-1.0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">if the Reason contradicts facts, subtract about </span><math id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">; if it clearly supports, add about </span><math id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">; generic </span><math id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">clip to </span><math id="A4.I2.i2.I1.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<span id="A4.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Do </span><span id="A4.I2.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">not</span><span id="A4.I2.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> reward verbosity; if the case is ambiguous, prefer </span><span id="A4.I2.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">neutral</span><span id="A4.I2.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and keep reward near </span><math id="A4.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I2.i3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A4.F13.pic1.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F13.pic1.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Return <span id="A4.F13.pic1.p5.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">only</span> the reward number (float). No JSON. No explanations.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A4.F13.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.F13.pic1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F13.pic1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">FULL trajectory (steps <math id="A4.F13.pic1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\dots T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\dots T</annotation></semantics></math>):</span><span id="A4.F13.pic1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span>
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A4.F13.pic1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{full_traj}</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A4.F13.pic1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.F13.pic1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F13.pic1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We are judging step <math id="A4.F13.pic1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\{t\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\{t\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A4.F13.pic1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.F13.pic1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F13.pic1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Student output (two lines):</span><span id="A4.F13.pic1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span>
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A4.F13.pic1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{student_two_lines}</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A4.F13.pic1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.F13.pic1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F13.pic1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Now output the reward number only.</span></span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 13: </span>Prompt template used for offline self-guidance model distillation.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Co-Evolving Improves the Self-Guidance Model</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We further examine whether co-evolving the self-guidance model with the policy improves the self-guidance model itself, rather than only the policy. To isolate this effect, we experiment on Webshop using Qwen3-1.7B. We fix the policy to <span id="A4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">checkpoint 40</span> and vary only the self-guidance model across different training checkpoints. If co-evolving indeed strengthens the self-guidance model, then later checkpoints should provide better guidance even for the same fixed policy.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ D.2 Co-Evolving Improves the Self-Guidance Model ‣ Appendix D Details of Offline Self-Guidance Model Distillation ‣ Co-Evolution of Policy and Internal Reward for Language Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> confirms this trend. Using <span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">checkpoint 10</span> as the self-guidance model yields a score of <span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">39.8</span> and a success rate of <span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">18.0%</span>, while replacing it with <span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">checkpoint 40</span> improves performance to <span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">51.2</span> and <span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">25.0%</span>. The best result is obtained with <span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">checkpoint 80</span>, which reaches a score of <span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">60.5</span> and a success rate of <span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">27.0%</span>. Since the policy is held fixed throughout this comparison, these gains cannot be attributed to policy improvement. Instead, they indicate that co-evolving during training progressively improves the self-guidance model itself.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Effect of self-guidance model checkpoints on a fixed policy. The policy is fixed to <span id="A4.T4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ckpt40</span>, while the self-guidance model is varied across training checkpoints.</figcaption>
<table id="A4.T4.4" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A4.T4.4.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.4.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Self-Guidance Model</td>
<td id="A4.T4.4.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Score</td>
<td id="A4.T4.4.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Success Rate (%)</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.4.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.4.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">checkpoint 10</td>
<td id="A4.T4.4.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">39.8</td>
<td id="A4.T4.4.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">18.0</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.4.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.4.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">checkpoint 40</td>
<td id="A4.T4.4.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">51.2</td>
<td id="A4.T4.4.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">25.0</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.4.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.4.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">checkpoint 80</td>
<td id="A4.T4.4.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="A4.T4.4.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">60.5</span></td>
<td id="A4.T4.4.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="A4.T4.4.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">27.0</span></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
